    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.bfs_tree - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.bfs_tree.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.bfs_tree()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Build the breadth-first search tree as a new graph.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.bfs_tree()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Build the breadth-first search tree as a new graph.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.bfs_tree()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Build the breadth-first search tree as a new graph.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nBuild the breadth-first search tree as a new graph.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L63942-L64036){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.bfs_tree(\n    source,\n    depth_limit=None,\n    mode=\"out\",\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![BFS tree](../assets/graphs/bfs-tree.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Left: a six-node graph with the root A outlined. Right: bfs_tree() returns a new directed graph keeping only the edges the breadth-first search discovered, A to B, A to C, B to D, B to E, and D to F, as accent arrows; the unused edges C-E and E-F are dashed. Every root path is a fewest-hops path, so the tree has depth 3.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nReturns the tree a breadth-first search from `source=` builds, as a directed graph with\nan edge from each node to every node it discovered (see `bfs_edges()`). Every path from\nthe root in this tree is a fewest-hops path in the original graph, which makes it handy\nfor drawing a network as levels around a focal node, for routing, or for reasoning\nabout distances as a tree.\n\nNodes keep their IDs, labels and attributes; each tree edge copies the weight and\nattributes of the original edge it follows. Nodes the search does not reach are left\nout.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[source]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Union[int, str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The root, as an integer ID or a string label.\n\n<code>[depth_limit]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Stop expanding at this many hops from the source. If `None` (default), there is no\n    limit.\n\n<code>[mode]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[&quot;out&quot;]{.st}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Which way to follow edges on a directed graph: `\"out\"` (default), `\"in\"`, or\n    `\"all\"`. Ignored for undirected graphs.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   A new directed graph: the BFS tree rooted at `source=`. The original graph is not\n    modified.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If the node does not exist, `depth_limit=` is negative, or `mode=` is invalid.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~bfs_edges`) \n\n:   The same edges as a list.\n\n[](`~dfs_tree`) \n\n:   The tree of a depth-first search.\n\n[](`~layout_bfs`) \n\n:   Draw a graph in layers by distance from a node.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nThe BFS tree of a 3 x 3 grid from a corner fans out along the rows and columns:\n\n::: {#ec5669b1 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngrid = ec.Graph().add_grid_2d(rows=3, cols=3)\ntree = grid.bfs_tree(1)\n\ntree.is_arborescence(), tree.count_edges()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n(True, 8)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Stops from Central\n\n`metro()` is a made-up city's metro network. Its BFS tree from Central keeps the stations'\nattributes, so it can be drawn in layers by `layout_bfs()`, one layer for each number of\nstops from Central:\n\n::: {#cef4edf1 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmetro = ec.metro()\ntree = metro.bfs_tree(\"Central\")\n\ntree.layout_bfs(\"Central\", attr_name=\"layers\").plot(\n    layout=\"layers\", label_by=\"label\"\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</style>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"700\" height=\"500\" viewBox=\"9.1 14.0 688.8 492.0\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<rect x=\"9.1\" y=\"14.0\" width=\"688.8\" height=\"492.0\" fill=\"var(--ect-3239c383)\"/>\n<g opacity=\"0.4\"><line x1=\"285.3\" y1=\"124.7\" x2=\"330.2\" y2=\"79.8\" stroke=\"var(--ect-e5dfd507)\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"338.7,71.3 332.9,82.5 327.5,77.1\" fill=\"var(--ect-e5dfd507)\"/></g>\n<line x1=\"285.3\" y1=\"124.7\" x2=\"338.7\" y2=\"71.3\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"transparent\" stroke-width=\"8.0\" pointer-events=\"stroke\" data-edge=\"11-12-0\" data-attrs='{\"id\": 10, \"edge\": \"Riverside \\u2192 Harbor\", \"weight\": 3.0, \"line\": \"Blue\", \"minutes\": 3}'/>\n<g opacity=\"0.4\"><line x1=\"285.3\" y1=\"375.3\" x2=\"330.2\" y2=\"420.2\" stroke=\"var(--ect-e5dfd507)\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"338.7,428.7 327.5,422.9 332.9,417.5\" fill=\"var(--ect